{
  "comment": [
    "Config / settings / retention / permissions / rotation / pricing.",
    "",
    "Schema and rules: see 00-foundation.json. One file per domain so the",
    "registry can be appended to in parallel; a duplicate code across two",
    "files is a hard error in the loader.",
    "",
    "Two entries in here carry safety semantics that a translator must not",
    "smooth over, both from AGENTS.md's \"Transcript retention\" section:",
    "",
    "  cc_retention.non_positive - `0` is NOT a short retention window. It",
    "    means write no transcripts and delete the existing ones at",
    "    startup, and it is reachable only through a separately named call",
    "    behind a type-to-confirm gate. This code exists so that value can",
    "    never be phrased as an ordinary out-of-range number.",
    "",
    "  cc_retention.write - the failure to persist a retention change. Its",
    "    remediation copy must never be \"restore the default\": a value CC's",
    "    schema rejects suppresses cleanup entirely, which *protects*",
    "    transcripts, so restoring re-arms deletion. That state is reported",
    "    as RetentionMode::Invalid, not as an error, and no code in this",
    "    file describes it.",
    "",
    "cc_env.invalid_enum_value / cc_env.invalid_number carry a `value`",
    "param. It is the user's env value, redacted at its one constructor",
    "(cc_env::settings::validate -> errors::redacted) and re-scanned in",
    "params(). ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS is marked secret in the spec",
    "precisely because it can carry an Authorization header; `name` is",
    "always safe to render, a value never is on its own authority."
  ],
